        {"after": "# Biodiversity — genetic, species, and ecosystem levels",
         "md": "**Biodiversity** is the totality of variation in life, measured at three nested levels: **genetic** (variation within a species — rice varieties, dog breeds), **species** (the variety of species in a region) and **ecosystem** (the variety of habitats — Terai grassland, hill forest, alpine meadow). It is the outcome of ~3.5 billion years of evolution, and it is currently being lost faster than at any time since the dinosaurs."},
